{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>For</b> — now he mentions men who were his friends and became his enemies." "<b>and I would bear</b> — his disgrace, for he is my enemy." "<b>he has magnified</b> — a verb, or הגדיל לדבר (he undertook to speak). The meaning: for a man can hide from an enemy, therefore only from an enemy who knows his secret."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 55, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:50.135593994Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}